ng sorry and the examination of the day","/study/curriculum/5/5-L3"],["lesson","8/8-7-3","Respect for life and the person","/study/curriculum/8/8-7-3"],["lesson","9/9-L1","Screens, comparison and who you are becoming","/study/curriculum/9/9-L1"],["lesson","K/K-1-3","God made me","/study/curriculum/K/K-1-3"],["lesson","11/11-10-1","Rites, sacramentals and popular devotion","/study/curriculum/11/11-10-1"],["reading","2026-08-02","Eighteenth Sunday In Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2026-08-02"],["reading","2026-09-20","Twenty-fifth Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2026-09-20"],["reading","2027-07-25","Seventeenth Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2027-07-25"],["reading","2028-05-14","Fifth Sunday of Easter","/pray/readings-together/2028-05-14"],["reading","2026-02-01","Fourth Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2026-02-01"],["reading","2027-09-05","Twenty-third Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2027-09-05"],["reading","2027-11-07","Thirty-second Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2027-11-07"],["reading","2026-01-09","Friday after Epiphany","/pray/readings-together/2026-01-09"],["reading","2026-06-07","The Solemnity of the Most Holy Body and Blood of Christ","/pray/readings-together/2026-06-07"],["reading","2027-01-08","Friday after Epiphany","/pray/readings-together/2027-01-08"],["reading","2027-02-07","Fifth Sunday in Ordinary Time","/pray/readings-together/2027-02-07"],["reading","2028-01-07","Friday after Epiphany","/pray/readings-together/2028-01-07"],["lesson","4/4-2-2","Angels and humans","/study/curriculum/4/4-2-2"],["lesson","3/3-8-2","Kinds of prayer","/study/curriculum/3/3-8-2"]],"why":["The Psalms are Israel’s prayer book and the Church’s.","Ordinary Time is the time of green, when we grow like plants in God’s love.","Psalm on 2028-01-03","A verse offered for this kind of hard day.","Nine- and ten-year-olds often cannot yet say what they feel, so feelings come out as stomachaches, shouting or silence.","Prayer is talking to God.","A verse to learn from this story.","The story, told for children.","God made us with a body and a soul.","A question children ask, with this verse in the answer.","Around twelve, feelings get stronger and less predictable.","The psalm lists refusing usury among the marks of the one who may dwell in God's sanctuary.","Why the Church once forbade lending at interest, and how that teaching changed.","Psalm on 2027-08-29","Psalm on 2026-04-19","Psalm on 2027-11-14","Psalm on 2026-10-25","Psalm on 2027-10-31","Didn’t the Church condemn Galileo and oppose science?","There’s no evidence for God.","Science has disproved the Bible; Genesis contradicts evolution.","Faith and reason are two wings by which the human spirit rises to the truth (Fides et Ratio).","The memory verse of this lesson.","God wants us to know him, so he speaks to us: in the beauty of creation, through the prophets, and most fully in his Son, Jesus.","From creation and the human person, reason can know that God exists.","The Church holds that faith and reason cannot contradict each other, since God is the author of both.","Psalm on 2028-01-23","Christians read Jesus into the Old Testament.","Almost everyone who prays seriously meets a time when nothing seems to happen, or when suffering or an argument makes belief feel foolish.","Psalm on 2026-03-29","Psalm on 2027-04-25","Jesus is the Good Shepherd who knows us and cares for us.","Many children lose a grandparent, a pet or a classmate by the age of ten.","Lectio divina is a way to pray with Scripture: read, meditate, pray, contemplate.","Most students will lose a grandparent, a pet, a friend or a classmate before they graduate.","God is our Father.","Fear in the dark, in a new place, at the doctor or at night is real for five-year-olds.","Psalm on 2026-03-15","Psalm on 2026-11-02","Psalm on 2027-07-18","Psalm on 2026-02-02","Psalm on 2026-11-01","Psalm on 2027-02-02","Psalm on 2028-02-02","Psalm on 2026-09-27","Psalm on 2027-11-28","The Middle Ages produced great cathedrals, universities and saints.","Psalm on 2026-01-25","Psalm on 2026-01-11","Psalm on 2028-01-09","Psalm on 2027-06-27","Psalm on 2028-04-30","Psalm on 2026-04-03","Psalm on 2028-04-14","Psalm on 2026-05-03","Psalm on 2027-05-23","Psalm on 2027-10-17","Psalm on 2027-08-08","Psalm on 2027-08-22","Psalm on 2026-01-18","Psalm on 2026-03-25","Psalm on 2027-01-17","Psalm on 2027-04-05","Psalm on 2028-03-25","Calling Mary the Queen of Heaven is pagan and takes glory from Christ.","We can pray in silence and listen to God.","Children at this age have screens, games, toys and noise everywhere.","Psalm on 2027-11-09","What the Church teaches about the first sin, and the passages it relies on.","Why should we be guilty for Adam’s sin?","The psalmist, confessing his own sin, sees it as reaching back to his very beginnings.","The Old Testament already speaks of sinfulness reaching back to the beginning of a person's life, not just to his own acts.","Many young people meet pornography early, and many carry secrecy and shame about it.","Sin wounds our relationship with God, ourselves and others; mercy heals.","The Church’s liturgy uses signs and symbols: water, oil, light, bread, wine, incense, gestures.","Sin is an offense against God and a wound to ourselves and others.","Psalm on 2026-02-22","There are five forms of prayer (blessing and adoration, petition, intercession, thanksgiving, praise) and three expressions (vocal, meditation,…","Many students say they do not know how to pray, or that prayer is boring, or that they forget.","Prayer is the raising of the mind and heart to God.","Psalm on 2026-11-08","Psalm on 2026-01-01","Psalm on 2026-08-16","Psalm on 2027-01-01","Psalm on 2028-01-01","Psalm on 2026-06-21","Psalm on 2028-01-30","Psalm on 2026-01-06","Psalm on 2026-01-07","Psalm on 2027-01-06","Psalm on 2026-09-14","Psalm on 2027-08-01","Psalm on 2027-09-14","Psalm on 2026-11-29","Psalm on 2027-12-19","Doubt is part of many people’s journey.","Everyone dies, yet we organise our lives to avoid thinking about it.","Angels are folk tales, and praying to your guardian angel is unbiblical.","What the Church teaches about angels who watch over us.","God gives each of us a guardian angel.","Angels are God’s helpers.","Psalm on 2028-03-05","Psalm on 2027-06-13","Psalm on 2028-02-27","Psalm on 2027-11-21","Worshipping a piece of bread is idolatry.","Psalm on 2026-03-08","Psalm on 2026-09-06","Psalm on 2027-01-31","Psalm on 2026-10-18","Psalm on 2026-08-06","Psalm on 2026-12-08","Psalm on 2027-12-08","We pray to praise God, to thank him, to ask for help and to say sorry.","Psalm on 2026-06-14","Psalm on 2028-05-07","Psalm on 2026-06-12","Psalm on 2026-09-13","Psalm on 2028-02-20","How the Church reads Genesis, and the verses cited in the Galileo case.","Catholics are either fundamentalists or they don’t believe the Bible.","Children love animals, plants and their own bodies.","God created everything out of nothing, freely and out of love.","Psalm on 2026-04-04","Psalm on 2027-03-27","Psalm on 2028-04-15","Why the Church calls the Mass a sacrifice, and how it relates to the one sacrifice of Calvary.","Psalm on 2026-02-08","Psalm on 2027-02-21","Psalm on 2027-05-30","Psalm on 2027-09-12","For many children, Sunday is just another busy day.","Sunday is the Lord’s Day, the day of Jesus’ Resurrection.","On Sunday we go to Mass.","Psalm on 2026-04-05","Psalm on 2026-04-12","Psalm on 2028-04-16","Psalm on 2028-04-23","Seven-year-olds are beginning to make real choices on their own.","The Liturgy of the Hours is the Church’s daily prayer.","Lectio divina is a slow, prayerful reading of a short passage in four movements: read (lectio), reflect (meditatio), respond (oratio), rest…","Psalm on 2026-02-15","The church is God’s house.","Psalm on 2027-10-24","The Church’s ban on contraception is out of date.","Why does the Church oppose IVF?","The Church teaches that children are a gift, not a product, and that science must serve the dignity of the person.","Psalm on 2026-11-15","Psalm on 2027-10-03","The 150 Psalms were the prayer book of Israel and of Jesus, and are the backbone of the Church’s daily prayer.","Psalm on 2026-03-22","Psalm on 2027-06-06","Many teenagers carry more stress than anyone admits: grades, friends, family, the future.","The Assumption is not in the Bible and was invented in 1950.","The Church's reasons for believing Mary was taken body and soul into heaven.","The psalm repeats hesed as a refrain after every act of God.","Babylon: The exiles sit by the rivers of Babylon and weep, and their captors ask them for songs.","Psalm on 2026-08-23","Psalm on 2028-02-06","The Bible does not mention abortion.","The Scripture the Church draws on to teach that life is sacred from conception.","People should have the right to die with dignity.","Scripture speaks of God's care for each person before birth.","God made each of us to know him, love him and be happy with him forever.","Every human life is a gift from conception to natural death, so direct abortion is gravely wrong.","The fifth commandment protects the dignity of human life from conception to natural death; the sixth, with the ninth, protects the dignity of the…","Every human life is sacred from conception to natural death because each person is made in God’s image.","Before Confession we think about what we did and ask God for help.","At ten and eleven, children begin to notice their changing bodies and to hear confused messages from peers and screens.","Fifth graders are preparing for deeper moral thinking and often for the Sacrament of Penance.","Your feed is built to make you compare, and comparison is the engine of envy.","God made me in a special way.","The Church celebrates in different rites, such as the Roman, Byzantine and Armenian, and uses sacramentals such as blessings, holy water and medals…","Psalm on 2026-08-02","Psalm on 2026-09-20","Psalm on 2027-07-25","Psalm on 2028-05-14","Psalm on 2026-02-01","Psalm on 2027-09-05","Psalm on 2027-11-07","Psalm on 2026-01-09","Psalm on 2026-06-07","Psalm on 2027-01-08","Psalm on 2027-02-07","Psalm on 2028-01-07","God made angels, pure spirits who serve and praise him, and humans, who are body and soul in the image of God.","The Church names five kinds of prayer: blessing and adoration, petition, intercession, thanksgiving and praise."],"notes":["The law forbids interest on loans to a poor fellow Israelite, and allows it with foreigners. The Fathers and councils applied this to Christians.","No verse says so. The Church points to Enoch and Elijah taken up, to the ark of the covenant, and to the woman in Revelation 12."],"topics":["Lending at interest","Original sin","Guardian angels","Creation and science","The Mass as sacrifice","The Assumption of Mary","The dignity of unborn life"],"r":{"1":[[0,0,0,60,0],[1,3,3,60,1]],"2":[[2,0,0,20,2]],"4":[[3,4,4,40,3],[4,8,8,60,4]],"5":[[5,2,3,60,5]],"8":[[6,1,1,40,6],[6,1,9,50,7],[7,0,0,60,8]],"13":[[8,1,1,60,9],[9,0,0,60,10]],"15":[[10,1,5,100,11],[10,5,5,90,12,0,0],[11,0,0,20,13]],"16":[[12,11,11,60,9],[13,0,0,20,14],[14,0,0,20,15]],"18":[[15,0,0,20,16],[16,0,0,20,17]],"19":[[17,1,6,80,18],[18,1,4,80,19],[19,1,1,80,20],[20,0,0,60,21],[20,1,1,40,22],[21,1,4,60,23],[22,1,1,40,22],[23,0,0,60,24],[23,1,1,40,22],[24,1,4,60,25],[24,1,1,40,22],[25,0,0,20,26]],"22":[[26,1,31,80,27],[27,1,5,60,28],[28,0,0,20,29],[29,0,0,20,30]],"23":[[30,4,4,60,9],[31,1,1,40,6],[31,1,6,50,7],[32,4,4,40,22],[33,0,0,60,31],[33,1,1,40,22],[34,0,0,60,32],[0,1,1,40,22],[35,0,0,60,33],[36,0,0,60,34],[37,1,1,60,35],[38,4,4,60,36],[39,0,0,20,37],[40,0,0,20,38],[41,0,0,20,39]],"24":[[42,0,0,20,40],[43,0,0,20,41],[44,0,0,20,42],[45,0,0,20,43]],"25":[[46,16,17,40,3],[47,0,0,20,44],[48,0,0,20,45]],"27":[[49,1,1,40,3],[50,10,10,60,9],[51,4,4,40,22],[51,4,4,60,46],[52,0,0,20,47]],"29":[[53,0,0,20,48],[54,0,0,20,49]],"30":[[55,0,0,20,50],[56,0,0,20,51]],"31":[[57,0,0,20,52],[58,